WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.807
I'm Simon Chamorro.

00:00:03.807 --> 00:00:06.880
I'm the co-founder and CEO of Valiu.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.730
And we're a product that
helps Venezuelans, living

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.900
in hyperinflation, protect
their money from losing value,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.180
receive remittances,

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.943
and pay locally to buy food and medicines.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.110
Both businesses and consumers
are able to exchange goods

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.590
and services with each other,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.152
paying in cryptocurrency.

00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:29.233
The vision for us is to
increase economic freedom.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.820
Venezuela is known

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.953
for its political and
economic instability.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.540
Hyperinflation has caused the Bolivar

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.230
to lose 99.9% of its value,

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.200
in just two years.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.720
Wealthy Venezuelan families
saw their fortunes disappear,

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.713
and the poor were pushed even
further into desperation.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.070
Simon Chamorro knows
this story all too well.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.630
Growing up in Venezuela,

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.390
essentially, wherever my dad

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.200
and my mom were able to build,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.090
during their life, was lost.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:09.360
When the economy started
to fail, we, for example

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.377
had water shortages or
like electricity blackouts

00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:14.830
across the country.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.343
Money was starting to get hyper inflated.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.390
This is not like a sad story
that I'm trying to tell.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.790
This is the reality of most Venezuelans.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.490
More than 99% of the Venezuelans

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.020
lost everything they've built,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.443
because the country failed.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.030
All of the Venezuelans savings

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.860
of most middle-class people went to zero,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.280
and I knew if I wanted to build something

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.900
I had to find my purpose.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.740
I always knew I wanted to start a company

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.860
and to build things,
which is the reason why

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:48.000
I studied industrial
design with the hypothesis

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.540
that I was going to be
able to build things.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.400
I didn't pursue that career,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.180
but I learned a lot of
things that got me into tech.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.410
So I found crypto through tech.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.170
I felt passionate about the technology.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.120
And then when I understood
the potential of crypto,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.810
I realized that Venezuela is potentially

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.873
the best place to do
this at a massive scale.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.970
The reality is, if we
deconstruct cryptocurrencies,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.370
the base, most basic thing is
that it helps disintermediate.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.900
And this may have the
possibility to change society

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.500
as we know it.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.520
The main problem Venezuelans are going

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.180
through right now is hyperinflation.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.380
Hyperinflation is just a byproduct

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.723
of total mismanagement of the country.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.150
Venezuela's descent into an
impoverished dictatorship

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.570
put the devastating
effects of hyperinflation

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.910
on full display for the world to see.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.630
Lines for basic needs,

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.650
extreme shortages of food
and medical supplies,

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.316
civil strife,

00:02:47.316 --> 00:02:48.320
violence,

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.450
and the citizens spared

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.210
were the ones who could
move their currency

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.960
out of Venezuela to other
more stable currencies,

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.370
like the US dollar,

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.670
a luxury mostly saved for the ultra elite.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.540
But Simon's platform, Valiu,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.770
promises the opportunity

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.310
for everyday Venezuelans
to protect themselves

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:08.150
from hyperinflation by
way of cryptocurrency.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.906
And according to him,

00:03:09.906 --> 00:03:10.739
the unstable conditions

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:13.210
of his country are the
perfect breeding ground

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.900
for such an experiment.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.260
Nobody trusts the currency
or the government.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.000
People are looking for solutions.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.650
In a place where people
are trying to survive,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:26.030
the barrier of trying
new things is much lower.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.200
So digital dollars,
Stablecoins, cryptocurrencies,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.220
people are going to be willing to try it

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.420
with a little bit of money

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.943
and then slowly kind of get there.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.220
Our main objective right
now as a company is to

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.900
enable merchants to accept digital dollars

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.910
as a medium of payment.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.898
And so people have to use the,

00:03:43.898 --> 00:03:46.223
the Bolivar less and less.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.530
We're focused on building
a product that serves

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:50.600
from the richest person,

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.630
with a lot of education
and technical literacy,

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.550
from the lowest income person,

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.910
with very low education
nd low technical literacy.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.040
In a country like Venezuela,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.124
where the minimum wage is one dollar,

00:04:02.124 --> 00:04:04.870
you have a situation where most people

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.950
are starting their own little business,

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:11.090
selling hot dogs or selling
the local food called, arepas,

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.730
or whatever they do,

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.360
but they sell it to their community.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.570
And you have these
hyper-local communities,

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.760
so we want to help them
accept payments in dollars in

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.290
in digital dollars and Stablecoins,

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.710
and then onboard users.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.750
The more consumers that pay in dollars,

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.690
the better for the merchants.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.530
The more merchants that accept it,

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.933
the better for the consumer.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.160
So far, we've moved millions of dollars,

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.670
we've helped more than 150,000 households,

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.850
30,000 monthly active
users and it's working.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:43.683
The reality is,

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.200
is that economic freedom

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.240
is only directly tackled

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.633
by the innovation that
is cryptocurrencies.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:54.340
But we can't forget that
Venezuela has tried this already.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:57.360
El Petro was a proposed
cryptocurrency backed

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.850
by the country's most
abundant resource, oil.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:04.530
While El Petro was widely
considered a resounding failure,

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.930
many experts agree that the
experiment was a necessary step

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:10.500
in establishing
cryptocurrency for the future.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.070
And Simon is convinced
that its foundations,

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.640
namely blockchain technology,
remains stronger than ever

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.513
and ready for another
more practical iteration.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.410
Blockchain is really a paradigm shift

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.020
for the human race.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.310
It's one of the most important things

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:30.920
that has happened in recent history.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:34.628
What you're starting to see, is companies

00:05:34.628 --> 00:05:38.490
starting to completely
build their products

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.990
on top of this blockchain.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.340
It's almost like it's
creating its own economy.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.930
If there's a way to provide more stability

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.580
and economic freedom and financial freedom

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:53.310
to Venezuelans without
crypto, I would rather

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.730
for that to happen, than
for me to be successful

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.763
with a product that doesn't
bring value to the people.

